These notes describe the variables contained in the attached three datasets and explain which datasets can be used to reproduce the Tables in the main text and the online appendix of "On Average Establishment Size across Sectors and Countries."

The three datasets (provided in Stata's .dta format) are Data_BRAES_Final.dta, Data_BRAES_indFinal.dta, and Data_BRAES_indRaw.dta.


*** Data_BRAES_Final.dta: This dataset can be used to reproduce the results in Tables 5, 6, and 7 in the main text.

Variables:
countrycode: 3-digit country code
gdp: GDP per capita, PPP
sizeM: average establishment size in the manufacturing sector
sizeS: average establishment size in the services sector
sizeNA: average establishment size in the non-agriculture sector
elasM: productivity elasticity of distortions in manufacturing
elasS: productivity elasticity of distortions in services
empM: population multiplied by employment share of manufacturing in non-agriculture
empS: population multiplied by employment share of services in non-agriculture
extfin: aggregate external financing relative to GDP
firing: firing costs
open: aggregate exports plus imports relative to GDP
sizeratio: average establishment size in manufacturing relative to services
empratio: share of employment in manufacturing relative to services
elasdiff: elasM minus elasS
ind_code: industry code
variables starting with an "l" are the natural log of the above


*** Data_BRAES_indFinal.dta: This dataset can be used to reproduce the results in Table 4 (Baseline column) in the main text.

Variables:
countrycode: 3-digit country code
gdp: GDP per capita, PPP
size: average establishment size
ind_code: industry code

