*** Data_BRAES_indRaw.dta: This dataset includes measures of average establishment size by industry using only raw data, as well as dummy variables signifying whether employees or persons engaged are used in the measure, whether firms or establishments are used in the measure, and whether nonemployers are used in the measure. This dataset can be used to reproduce the results in Table 4 (Raw column) in the main text, and Tables 3 and 4 in the Online Appendix.

Variables:
countrycode: 3-digit country code
gdp: GDP per capita, PPP
sizeM: average establishment size or average firm size in this country's manufacturing sector
sizeS: average establishment size or average firm size
elasM: productivity elasticity of distortions in manufacturing
elasS: productivity elasticity of distortions in services
empM: population multiplied by employment share of manufacturing in non-agriculture
empS: population multiplied by employment share of services in non-agriculture
extfin: aggregate external financing relative to GDP
firing: firing costs
open: aggregate exports plus imports relative to GDP
sizeratio: average establishment size in manufacturing relative to this industry
empratio: share of employment in manufacturing relative to services
elasdiff: elasM minus elasS
ind_code: industry code
ifemp: equals 1 if sizeS is calculated using employment (rather than persons engaged), 0 otherwise
ifempM: equals 1 if sizeM is calculated using employment (rather than persons engaged), 0 otherwise
iffirm: equals 1 if sizeS is calculated using firms (rather than establishments), 0 otherwise
iffirmM: equals 1 if sizeM is calculated using firms (rather than establishments), 0 otherwise
firm1: equals 1 if sizeS is calculated without including nonemployers, 0 otherwise
firm1M: equals 1 if sizeM is calculated without including nonemployers, 0 otherwise

